sycl: apply the per-expert weight scale of MUL_MAT_ID in one kernel

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0023.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

NVFP4 checkpoints carry one weight scale per expert. llama.cpp applies it
after each MUL_MAT_ID as a RESHAPE, a REPEAT, a GET_ROWS by the expert ids
and a MUL: four nodes, three kernels, per projection. The chain (the shape
CUDA matches in ggml_cuda_get_mul_mat_id_scale) now runs as one kernel after
the MUL_MAT_ID that reads the scale by the id directly. graph_optimize keeps
the ids allocated until the MUL; 0023 then matches the reduction at the
second MUL. Inkling scales both expert projections (gate_up and down) of
its 44 MoE passes per token: 88 chains, 176 fewer kernels per token.
test-backend-ops covers it in MUL_MAT_FUSION.

